---
/**
 * The quick start wizard.
 *
 * Five steps, one output. The client script imports the same generator the
 * Install page uses, so there is one Compose template rather than two, and Vite
 * bundles it into the page.
 *
 * Everything happens in the browser. No fetch, no analytics, no secret: the
 * generated script calls `openssl rand` on the target machine, so nothing
 * sensitive exists here to leak.
 *
 * Design: existing --q-* tokens from styles/theme.css only. No new colours.
 */
---

<div class="qs" data-quickstart>
	<ol class="qs-progress" aria-label="Progress">
		<li data-dot="1" class="on">Host</li>
		<li data-dot="2">GPU</li>
		<li data-dot="3">Storage</li>
		<li data-dot="4">Owner</li>
		<li data-dot="5">Access</li>
		<li data-dot="6">Result</li>
	</ol>

	<!-- 1. Platform -->
	<section data-step="1" class="qs-step on">
		<h2>Where are you deploying Quasar?</h2>
		<p class="qs-hint">
			This sets sensible defaults later, and it changes how the script makes
			things survive a reboot.
		</p>
		<div class="qs-choices">
			<label><input type="radio" name="platform" value="fedora" checked /><span><strong>Fedora</strong><em>What the install is verified on</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="platform" value="debian" /><span><strong>Debian or Ubuntu</strong></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="platform" value="arch" /><span><strong>Arch</strong></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="platform" value="unraid" /><span><strong>Unraid</strong><em>Different paths, different persistence</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="platform" value="other" /><span><strong>Another systemd Linux</strong></span></label>
		</div>
		<p class="qs-note" data-platform-note></p>
	</section>

	<!-- 2. GPU -->
	<section data-step="2" class="qs-step">
		<h2>What GPU does this machine have?</h2>
		<p class="qs-hint">This selects GPU access. The agent detects the encoder automatically.</p>
		<div class="qs-choices">
			<label><input type="radio" name="gpu" value="amd-intel" checked /><span><strong>AMD or Intel</strong><em>Automatic encoder</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="gpu" value="nvidia" /><span><strong>NVIDIA</strong><em>Vulkan Video</em></span></label>
		</div>
		<p class="qs-note" data-when-gpu="amd-intel">
			The agent detects your GPU and selects its default encoder. Advanced
			operators can override <code>QUASAR_ENCODER</code> in the environment file.
		</p>
		<p class="qs-note" data-when-gpu="nvidia">
			You need the NVIDIA driver and <code>nvidia-container-toolkit</code>
			installed and registered with Docker first. The generated script checks
			that runtime without restarting your other containers.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- 3. Storage -->
	<section data-step="3" class="qs-step">
		<h2>Where should Quasar keep things?</h2>
		<p class="qs-hint">
			User homes hold game saves, settings and launcher downloads. Templates
			live beside the homes. Certificates, artwork and the database use Docker-managed
			volumes, so the installer does not need to change their host ownership.
		</p>
		<label class="qs-field">
			<span>Base path</span>
			<input type="text" name="basePath" value="/var/lib/quasar" spellcheck="false" />
		</label>
		<label class="qs-check">
			<input type="checkbox" name="separateSaves" />
			<span>Keep user homes on a different disk</span>
		</label>
		<label class="qs-field" data-when-saves>
			<span>Path for user homes</span>
			<input type="text" name="savesPath" placeholder="/mnt/tank/quasar" spellcheck="false" />
		</label>

		<figure class="qs-tree">
			<figcaption>What you end up with</figcaption>
			<pre data-tree></pre>
		</figure>
	</section>

	<!-- 4. Owner -->
	<section data-step="4" class="qs-step">
		<h2>Who should own your save data?</h2>
		<p class="qs-hint">
			Game containers drop to this user, so it decides who can read the saves
			from outside Quasar. It does not change what the node agent runs as: that
			is root, because it needs the Docker socket and the input devices.
		</p>
		<div class="qs-choices">
			<label><input type="radio" name="owner" value="dedicated" checked /><span><strong>The default for this host</strong><em data-owner-default>uid 1000</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="owner" value="custom" /><span><strong>A specific uid and gid</strong><em>If your files need to belong to an existing account</em></span></label>
		</div>
		<div class="qs-row" data-when-owner="custom">
			<label class="qs-field"><span>uid</span><input type="number" name="uid" value="1000" min="0" /></label>
			<label class="qs-field"><span>gid</span><input type="number" name="gid" value="1000" min="0" /></label>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- 5. Access -->
	<section data-step="5" class="qs-step">
		<h2>How will you reach Quasar?</h2>
		<p class="qs-hint">
			Quasar needs HTTPS. Gamepads, Escape capture and the microphone all need
			a secure context.
		</p>
		<div class="qs-choices">
			<label><input type="radio" name="access" value="self-signed" checked /><span><strong>Let Quasar make a certificate</strong><em>The default. Right for a LAN</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="access" value="proxy" /><span><strong>I already have a reverse proxy</strong><em>Caddy, Traefik, nginx already running</em></span></label>
			<label><input type="radio" name="access" value="own-cert" /><span><strong>I have my own certificate</strong><em>From an internal or public CA</em></span></label>
		</div>

		<div data-when-access="self-signed">
			<label class="qs-field qs-required">
				<span>What addresses will you type into the browser?</span>
				<input type="text" name="tlsHosts" placeholder="192.168.1.50,quasar.lan" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<p class="qs-note">
				Every IP and hostname, comma separated. The certificate is generated
				once on first boot and names exactly these. Leave one out and that
				address gives you <code>ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID</code>, which
				cannot be clicked through, because the certificate does not claim that
				address at all.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div data-when-access="proxy">
			<label class="qs-field qs-required">
				<span>Public URL your proxy serves</span>
				<input type="text" name="publicUrl" placeholder="https://quasar.example.com" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<label class="qs-field">
				<span>Addresses for direct LAN access, if you still want it</span>
				<input type="text" name="tlsHostsProxy" placeholder="192.168.1.50" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<p class="qs-note qs-warn">
				Your proxy carries login and signaling. It does not carry the stream.
				Video is WebRTC straight from the GPU host to the browser, so the two
				still need a direct route: a LAN or a VPN. Publishing the login page
				does not publish the stream.
			</p>
			<label class="qs-field">
				<span>Which proxy?</span>
				<select name="proxy">
					<option value="caddy">Caddy</option>
					<option value="traefik">Traefik</option>
					<option value="nginx">nginx</option>
					<option value="npm">NGINX Proxy Manager</option>
				</select>
			</label>
		</div>

		<div data-when-access="own-cert">
			<label class="qs-field qs-required">
				<span>Certificate file on this host</span>
				<input type="text" name="certPath" placeholder="/etc/ssl/quasar/fullchain.pem" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<label class="qs-field qs-required">
				<span>Private key file</span>
				<input type="text" name="keyPath" placeholder="/etc/ssl/quasar/privkey.pem" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<label class="qs-field">
				<span>Addresses for direct access</span>
				<input type="text" name="tlsHostsCert" placeholder="192.168.1.50,quasar.lan" spellcheck="false" />
			</label>
			<p class="qs-note">
				The certificate needs every browser-facing name as a subject
				alternative name, with IP addresses as IP SANs. Browsers ignore the
				common name. Include the full chain leaf first, and use an unencrypted
				key: there is nowhere to type a passphrase at boot.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- 6. Result -->
	<section data-step="6" class="qs-step">
		<h2>Your install</h2>
		<dl class="qs-summary">
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>Host</dt><dd data-sum="platform"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>GPU</dt><dd data-sum="gpu"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>Base path</dt><dd data-sum="base"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>User homes</dt><dd data-sum="homes"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>Owned by</dt><dd data-sum="owner"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row"><dt>Access</dt><dd data-sum="access"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row" data-sum-row="tls"><dt>Certificate names</dt><dd data-sum="tls"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row" data-sum-row="public"><dt>Public URL</dt><dd data-sum="public"></dd></div>
			<div class="qs-sum-row" data-sum-row="proxy"><dt>Proxy</dt><dd data-sum="proxy"></dd></div>
		</dl>

		<details class="qs-adv">
			<summary>Change the ports</summary>
			<div class="qs-row">
				<label class="qs-field"><span>HTTP</span><input type="number" name="controlPort" value="8080" min="1" max="65535" /></label>
				<label class="qs-field"><span>HTTPS</span><input type="number" name="tlsPort" value="8443" min="1" max="65535" /></label>
			</div>
		</details>

		<div class="qs-out">
			<div class="qs-out-head">
				<h3>Run this on the host</h3>
				<button type="button" data-copy="script">Copy</button>
			</div>
			<p class="qs-hint">
				Read it before you run it. It writes two files, sets one sysctl, loads
				the uinput module and starts the stack. The three secrets are generated
				on that machine by the script, so nothing sensitive came from this page.
			</p>
			<pre><code data-out="script"></code></pre>
		</div>

		<div class="qs-out" data-out-block="proxy" hidden>
			<div class="qs-out-head">
				<h3>Add to your <span data-out="proxyName"></span> config</h3>
				<button type="button" data-copy="proxy">Copy</button>
			</div>
			<p class="qs-hint">
				Goes in <code data-out="proxyFile"></code>. This adds Quasar to a proxy
				you already run; it does not stand one up.
			</p>
			<pre><code data-out="proxy"></code></pre>
		</div>

		<details class="qs-adv">
			<summary>The individual files, if you would rather write them yourself</summary>
			<div class="qs-out-head"><h4>deploy/docker-compose.yml</h4><button type="button" data-copy="compose">Copy</button></div>
			<pre><code data-out="compose"></code></pre>
			<div data-out-block="nvidia" hidden>
				<div class="qs-out-head"><h4>deploy/docker-compose.nvidia.yml</h4><button type="button" data-copy="nvidia">Copy</button></div>
				<pre><code data-out="nvidia"></code></pre>
			</div>
			<p class="qs-hint">Replace the blank credentials with real values using the instructions in this file before starting. Paste command output, not shell commands.</p>
			<div class="qs-out-head"><h4>deploy/.env</h4><button type="button" data-copy="env">Copy</button></div>
			<pre><code data-out="env"></code></pre>
		</details>

		<p class="qs-hint">
			Then open Quasar and continue with
			<a href="/quasar/install/first-run/">first-run setup</a>. Prefer to read
			the whole thing instead? <a href="/quasar/install/install/">Install
			Quasar</a> covers the same ground as prose.
		</p>
	</section>

	<nav class="qs-nav">
		<button type="button" data-back disabled>Back</button>
		<span class="qs-count"><span data-current>1</span> of 6</span>
		<button type="button" data-next>Next</button>
	</nav>
</div>

<script>
	import { DEFAULTS, generate, homePath } from '../data/stack-template.js';
	import { platform } from '../data/platforms.js';

	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-quickstart]')) {
		const PROXY_NAMES = { caddy: 'Caddy', traefik: 'Traefik', nginx: 'nginx', npm: 'NGINX Proxy Manager' };
		const answers = { ...DEFAULTS };
		let step = 1;
		const LAST = 6;
		// Only overwrite a path or uid the reader has not typed into themselves.
		const touched = new Set();

		const $ = (sel) => root.querySelector(sel);
		const $$ = (sel) => Array.from(root.querySelectorAll(sel));
		const field = (name) => root.querySelector(`[name="${name}"]`);

		/** Read every control into the answers object. */
		function collect() {
			const val = (n) => field(n)?.value?.trim() ?? '';
			answers.platform = root.querySelector('[name="platform"]:checked')?.value ?? 'fedora';
			answers.gpu = root.querySelector('[name="gpu"]:checked')?.value ?? 'amd-intel';
			answers.owner = root.querySelector('[name="owner"]:checked')?.value ?? 'dedicated';
			answers.access = root.querySelector('[name="access"]:checked')?.value ?? 'self-signed';
			answers.basePath = val('basePath') || platform(answers.platform).defaultBasePath;
			answers.separateSaves = field('separateSaves')?.checked ?? false;
			answers.savesPath = val('savesPath');
			answers.uid = Number(val('uid') || platform(answers.platform).defaultUid);
			answers.gid = Number(val('gid') || platform(answers.platform).defaultGid);
			answers.proxy = val('proxy') || 'caddy';
			answers.publicUrl = val('publicUrl');
			answers.certPath = val('certPath');
			answers.keyPath = val('keyPath');
			answers.controlPort = Number(val('controlPort') || 8080);
			answers.tlsPort = Number(val('tlsPort') || 8443);
			// One answer, three inputs: whichever branch is showing owns it.
			answers.tlsHosts =
				answers.access === 'proxy'
					? val('tlsHostsProxy')
					: answers.access === 'own-cert'
						? val('tlsHostsCert')
						: val('tlsHosts');
		}

		/**
		 * Move the defaults to match the platform, unless the reader has typed
		 * their own value into that field. Unraid wants /mnt/user/appdata and
		 * uid 99, and guessing wrong there is worse than not guessing at all.
		 */
		function applyPlatformDefaults() {
			const p = platform(answers.platform);
			if (!touched.has('basePath')) field('basePath').value = p.defaultBasePath;
			if (!touched.has('uid')) field('uid').value = String(p.defaultUid);
			if (!touched.has('gid')) field('gid').value = String(p.defaultGid);
			const note = $('[data-platform-note]');
			note.textContent = p.note;
			note.hidden = !p.note;
			$('[data-owner-default]').textContent = p.ownerLabel;
		}

		/**
		 * A picture of the directories, because "base path" and "save data path"
		 * mean nothing until you see what lands in each.
		 */
		function tree() {
			const homes = homePath(answers);
			// Pad to one column so the comments line up whatever the nesting depth.
			const row = (path, comment) => (comment ? `${path.padEnd(26)}${comment}` : path);
			const lines = [
				`${homes}/`,
				row('  alice/', 'one directory per user'),
				row('    steam/', 'library, saves and settings'),
				row('  bob/', ''),
				'',
				`${homes.replace(/\/[^/]*$/, '/templates')}/`,
				row('  …', 'prepared application homes'),
				'',
				'Docker-managed volumes:',
				row('  quasar-control-tls', 'certificate and artwork cache'),
				row('  quasar-postgres-data', 'accounts and configuration'),
			];
			$('[data-tree]').textContent = lines.join('\n');
		}

		/** Show and hide the conditional blocks. */
		function reveal() {
			$$('[data-when-gpu]').forEach((el) => {
				el.hidden = el.dataset.whenGpu !== answers.gpu;
			});
			$$('[data-when-owner]').forEach((el) => {
				el.hidden = el.dataset.whenOwner !== answers.owner;
			});
			$$('[data-when-access]').forEach((el) => {
				el.hidden = el.dataset.whenAccess !== answers.access;
			});
			const saves = $('[data-when-saves]');
			if (saves) saves.hidden = !answers.separateSaves;
		}

		/**
		 * The required field on the access step is the whole reason this wizard
		 * exists, so Next stays disabled until it has a value. Nothing else blocks.
		 */
		const ACCESS_STEP = 5;
		function stepComplete(n) {
			if (n !== ACCESS_STEP) return true;
			if (answers.access === 'self-signed') return answers.tlsHosts.length > 0;
			if (answers.access === 'proxy') return answers.publicUrl.length > 0;
			return answers.certPath.length > 0 && answers.keyPath.length > 0;
		}

		function summary() {
			const p = platform(answers.platform);
			const gpuName = { 'amd-intel': 'AMD or Intel', nvidia: 'NVIDIA' }[answers.gpu];
			const accessName = {
				'self-signed': 'Certificate generated by Quasar',
				proxy: 'Behind your own reverse proxy',
				'own-cert': 'Your own certificate',
			}[answers.access];

			const set = (k, v) => ($(`[data-sum="${k}"]`).textContent = v);
			set('platform', p.label);
			set('gpu', gpuName);
			set('base', answers.basePath);
			set('homes', homePath(answers));
			set('owner', `uid ${answers.uid}, gid ${answers.gid}`);
			set('access', accessName);
			set('tls', answers.tlsHosts);
			set('public', answers.publicUrl);
			set('proxy', PROXY_NAMES[answers.proxy] ?? '');

			$('[data-sum-row="tls"]').hidden = !answers.tlsHosts;
			$('[data-sum-row="public"]').hidden = answers.access !== 'proxy' || !answers.publicUrl;
			$('[data-sum-row="proxy"]').hidden = answers.access !== 'proxy';
		}

		function render() {
			collect();
			applyPlatformDefaults();
			collect();
			reveal();
			tree();
			const out = generate(answers);

			$('[data-out="script"]').textContent = out.script;
			$('[data-out="compose"]').textContent = out.compose;
			$('[data-out="env"]').textContent = out.env;

			const nvBlock = $('[data-out-block="nvidia"]');
			nvBlock.hidden = !out.nvidia;
			if (out.nvidia) $('[data-out="nvidia"]').textContent = out.nvidia;

			const pxBlock = $('[data-out-block="proxy"]');
			pxBlock.hidden = !out.proxyConfig;
			if (out.proxyConfig) {
				$('[data-out="proxy"]').textContent = out.proxyConfig.body;
				$('[data-out="proxyName"]').textContent = out.proxyConfig.name;
				$('[data-out="proxyFile"]').textContent = out.proxyConfig.filename;
			}

			summary();
			$('[data-next]').disabled = step === LAST || !stepComplete(step);
			$('[data-back]').disabled = step === 1;
			$('[data-current]').textContent = String(step);
		}

		function show(n) {
			step = Math.min(LAST, Math.max(1, n));
			$$('[data-step]').forEach((el) => el.classList.toggle('on', Number(el.dataset.step) === step));
			$$('[data-dot]').forEach((el) => el.classList.toggle('on', Number(el.dataset.dot) <= step));
			render();
			root.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
		}

		root.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
			if (e.target?.name) touched.add(e.target.name);
			render();
		});
		root.addEventListener('change', render);
		$('[data-next]').addEventListener('click', () => show(step + 1));
		$('[data-back]').addEventListener('click', () => show(step - 1));

		$$('[data-copy]').forEach((btn) => {
			btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
				const text = $(`[data-out="${btn.dataset.copy}"]`).textContent;
				try {
					await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
					const was = btn.textContent;
					btn.textContent = 'Copied';
					setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = was), 1600);
				} catch {
					btn.textContent = 'Select it and copy';
				}
			});
		});

		show(1);
	}
</script>

<style>
	.qs {
		border: 1px solid var(--q-line-2, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
		border-radius: var(--q-r-lg, 12px);
		background: var(--q-ink-2, oklch(0.163 0.018 268));
		padding: 1.5rem;
		margin: 1.75rem 0;
	}

	.qs-progress {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
		padding: 0;
		font-family: var(--q-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.6875rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	/* Starlight puts 0.25rem between list items inside markdown content, which
	   pushed every step but the first down by 4px and left the first bar
	   floating above the row. */
	.qs-progress li + li {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.qs-progress li {
		flex: 1;
		padding-top: 0.5rem;
		border-top: 2px solid var(--q-line-2, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
		color: var(--q-text-4, oklch(0.56 0.024 259));
	}
	.qs-progress li.on {
		border-top-color: var(--sl-color-accent, oklch(0.5998 0.2179 273.21));
		color: var(--q-text-2, oklch(0.76 0.022 258));
	}

	.qs-step {
		display: none;
	}
	.qs-step.on {
		display: block;
	}
	.qs-step h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}

	.qs-hint {
		color: var(--q-text-3, oklch(0.6605 0.0265 259.81));
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.qs-choices {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.qs-choices label {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: baseline;
		padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--q-line-2, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12));
		border-radius: var(--q-r-md, 10px);
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.qs-choices label:has(input:checked) {
		border-color: var(--sl-color-accent, oklch(0.5998 0.2179 273.21));
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-accent, oklch(0.5998 0.2179 273.21)) 8%, transparent);
	}
	.qs-choices span {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.15rem;
	}
	.qs-choices em {
		font-style: normal;
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		color: var(--q-text-3, oklch(0.6605 0.0265 259.81));
	}

	.qs-field {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
	}
	.qs-field > span {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}
	.qs-field input,
	.qs-field select {
